<node id="Systemic Inflammatory Response Syndrome (SIRS) / Sepsis">
  <data key="d0">mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">A dysregulated host response to infection or injury, characterized by widespread inflammation leading to endothelial dysfunction, vasodilation, capillary leak, and potentially organ failure. In severe cases, it progresses to septic shock.</data>
  <data key="d2">25</data>
</node>
